<%# `hidden` is the initial state; `admin--save-bar#refresh` toggles it. The
    count is a polite live region so a screen reader hears the number change.
    Full-bleed: the form that holds the bar is usually a narrow column, so
    `admin--save-bar` gives the bar negative side margins that reach the
    edges of `<main>` (`bleed`) -- no fixed `-mx-` here would be right for
    every column. %>
<div hidden data-admin--save-bar-target="bar" class="admin-save-bar sticky bottom-0 z-20 mt-6 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 border-t border-line bg-surface px-6 py-3">
  <span data-admin--save-bar-target="count" aria-live="polite" class="mr-auto text-[13px] text-dim"></span>
  <%= link_to "Cancel", cancel_url, data: { turbo_frame: "content" }, class: setup_secondary_link_class %>
  <%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: save_label, variant: :primary, type: "submit", form: form_id, data: save_data) %>
</div>
<%# The bar above starts `hidden` and only `admin--save-bar` ever shows it, so
    without JavaScript the form would have no submit button at all. This one
    exists only then (a browser with scripting on never parses it into the
    page), the way the filter forms keep their "Filter" button. %>
<noscript><%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: save_label, variant: :primary, type: "submit", form: form_id) %></noscript>
